The members is a list of 2, 3, and 5.
The gains is a list of 6, 7, and 8.
The people is 10.
The target is 5.
The width is target plus 1.
The rows is (people plus 1) times width.
The table is a list of 264 zeros.
Set item 0 of table to 1.
For every crime from 0 to 2.
The cost is item crime of members.
The gain is item crime of gains.
For every used from 0 to people.
For every earned from 0 to target.
The here is crime times rows plus used times width plus earned.
The next is here plus rows.
Set item next of table to item next of table plus item here of table.
If used plus cost is at most people.
The reached is earned plus gain.
If reached is more than target, set reached to target.
The moved is next plus cost times width plus reached minus earned.
Set item moved of table to item moved of table plus item here of table.

The total is 0.
For every used from 0 to people.
Set total to total plus item (3 times rows plus used times width plus target) of table.

Show total.
